# CODEOWNERS — path-scoped merge authority (reference §7.3, §7.10)
#
# Each working-group folder is owned by exactly TWO leads, one from each of two
# DIFFERENT partner companies. CODEOWNERS enforces "a code owner must approve";
# the cross-company constraint is additionally enforced by a required GitHub
# Actions check (see .github/workflows/) because CODEOWNERS alone cannot verify
# that two approvers belong to different partner teams.
#
# Replace the @org/team placeholders below with real GitHub teams once the org
# and per-partner teams exist. Every contributor belongs to exactly one partner
# team (reference §4 / tooling proposal item 5).

# --- Community-level governance: owned by the conveners ---
/reference/            @OWNER-ORG/conveners
/governance/           @OWNER-ORG/conveners
/README.md             @OWNER-ORG/conveners
/LICENSE               @OWNER-ORG/conveners
/.github/              @OWNER-ORG/conveners

# --- Chapters: owned by the chapter's council ---
/chapters/brazil/      @OWNER-ORG/brazil-council
/chapters/us/          @OWNER-ORG/us-council

